welcome to thick boy fighters let's dive  in in a video posted to instagram  heavyweight tom aspinall gave his fans  an update on his knee injury aspinall  injured the knee last saturday 15  seconds into his main event fight with  curtis blades aspinall detailed the next  step of his recovery which include an  mri scan and surgery  hello everybody  just a quick update on the knee  situation  because plenty of people are asking  about the diagnosis of what happened to  the knee  now anybody who's got knee problems  knows  that in order to have an mri scan an  accurate mri scan  you need to let the swelling go down  so i spoke to the surgeon  we have a rough idea of what it is  but  we are currently waiting for the  swelling to go down  and i will be having the mri scan this  weekend and having surgery  early next week in london  so just want to say massive thank you to  everyone who's reached out obviously  i've been offline been down in the dumps  since saturday night but  hopefully  we'll uh  get it fixed get the surgery early next  week thank you francis nagano's coach  eric nixik gave an update on naganu's  recovery while appearing on mma junkie  according to nick six comments it may  not be much longer until fans see the  heavyweight champ fighting again  i think he's either ahead of schedule or  on track one or the other and from what  i've gathered he's making great strides  he's back in the gym moving around  hitting pads and stuff nick sick  continued by sharing the most difficult  thing about coaching the ganu through  the injury the biggest thing for me as a  coach what i miss out on is time of  growing areas that we can improve on  that's where i get like oh man we're not  doing enough x y z and i'm okay with  that we don't have a fight lined up or  anything right now his main focus is  getting his knee rehab to the point  where he can get back in the lab and  start doing these things again hopefully  and it sounds like for what he's saying  that if something were to happen it  would be the end of the year or early  2023.  on wednesday the abc association of  boxing and combative sports passed two  changes to the unified rules of mma the  two changes were voted on at the 2022  abc conference and passed unanimously  the first rule change increased the  recovery time for fighters dealing with  an eye poke fighters will now be granted  five minutes to recover after an eye  poke the same amount of time allotted  for drawing strikes if the fighter is  not ready after five minutes expire the  fight will be called off the second rule  change allows for neoprene sleeves to be  worn by competitors mma junkie reported  the official rule change to be  a competitor may use soft neoprene type  sleeves to cover only the knee or ankle  joints approved sleeves may not have  padding velcro plastic metal ties or any  materials considered to be unsafe or  that may create an unfair advantage  neoprene sleeves are not considered  equipment or clothing and may not be  grabbed advantageously inside or as  clothing that can be grabbed by self  tape and gauze or any materials other  than the approved sleeves are not  permitted on the lower body the sleeves  must be black in color with the  exception of matching the athlete's  commission assigned corners with the  sleeves being blue or red or colored as  appropriate at the ufc 277 pre-fight  press conference ahead of his interim  title bout against brandon moreno kai  kara france spoke about the last time he  shared the octagon with moreno a  decision lost at ufc 245  you know the car that fought brandon  back in 2019 is in the same car they're  standing in front of you today  i've got so much more experience now  being a father being a husband i've got  more purpose and i'm just on another  level so you know congrats for brandon  for what he's done since we've fought  you know going on to win the title uh  but it's my time so you know  you know dallas texas i love being out  here you know i'm a long way from home  but i'll show you why i'm the best in  the world when asked whether he expects  a different version of the moreno he  previously fought kaikoura france  responded  you know brandon's the most dangerous  weapon is his mindset you know this  guy's a dog and i expect it to be a dog  fight so  comes here today we'll find out  at the press conference amanda nunez  laid out her plan to defend her  featherweight belt if she defeats the  bantamweight champion giuliana pena on  saturday when asked whether she would  consider challenging nunez for the 145  pound belt pena responded all the real  fights are at 135 she's saying that she  is going to fight at 145 and defend her  belt against who name three 145ers name  two 145ers there's nobody in that  division everybody knows the real fights  are at 135 pounds amanda and i are the  two best female fighters in the world  and all the real [ __ ] is at 1 35. pena  then gave a graphic description for what  fans can expect tomorrow night when the  octagon door closes i'm going to punch  kick pull her hair i'm going to bite her  i'm going to gouge her eyeballs out if i  have to i'm literally going to do  everything in there trust me when i say  i'm willing to die and do whatever it  takes i'm going to do whatever it takes  the ufc 277 weigh-ins were held friday  with all fighters on the main card  making weight women's bantamweight  champion juliana pena made a stir when  she waited until the last 90 seconds of  the weigh-in window to step on the scale  video courtesy of mma junkie the ufc  bantamweight champion the venezuelan  vixen julianna  [Music]  two early prelim fighters however did  not make their weight orion kosei  weighed two and a half pounds over his  170 pound limit and will forfeit 20  percent of his purse in his bout against  mike mathetha jocelyn edwards missed her  135 pound limit when she tipped the  scales at 137 and a half pounds she will  also forfeit 20 of her purse during his  visit to thick boys studios ufc  lightweight contender michael chandler  gave his exclusive picks for ufc 277 to  the thick boy fight news team  you can never bet against the beast  derrick lewis he's the man pavlovich is  very tough he's surging and i'm taking  derrick lewis kykar of france versus  brandon moreno brandon moreno being the  former champion this is for the antrim  belt never bet against kai kar francis  he's a tough kiwi from new zealand but i  think brandon moreno is just too  confident too good everywhere moreno  gets it done julianna pena versus amanda  nunes how do you ever  say that that that wasn't a fluke on the  first one so many people pena has came  out won the title but goodness gracious  amanda nunes has looked and been the  most dominant female fighter that we've  ever seen i'm going i think amanda nunes  gets her title back looking for more  original mma content check out the rest  of thick boy youtube exclusive  interviews opinion and fight analysis is  available weekly on the shob show food  truck diaries and fight night flashbacks  subscribe so you don't miss any of the  action  you
 

